    "body": "It is meant to be an actual condition, and the parentheses were meant to help with grouping to make it clear what the condition applied to.  I've restructured the comma-separated list as a `<ul class=brief>` and avoided the parentheses, which might be better.\r\n\r\nI suppose an alternative is to drop the parameter and pull out the list of conditions (bdi element, script element, etc.) into its own definition (e.g., \"auto-directionality traversal excluded element\") and then refer to that definition from two places (the current location and the place where `true` is passed).  (The thing I was really trying to avoid was duplicating that list.)",
